 in cultural activities and celebrations in this authentic island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Alifushi has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and authentic cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Alifushi Island?","answer":"Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Raa Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Alifushi?","answer":"The best time to visit Alifushi is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more authentic local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Alifushi?","answer":"Alifushi offers various budget-friendly accommodations including authentic guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a genuine setting."},{"question":"What makes Alifushi''s community special?","answer":"Alifushi is known for its authentic and genuine community atmosphere. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while welcoming visitors with warm hospitality. Visitors can experience real cultural exchanges and participate in community activities in this traditional setting."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["rasgetheemu","ungoofaaru","rasmaadhoo","vaadhoo","angolhitheemu","dhuvaafaru","fainu","hulhudhuffaaru","inguraidhoo","innamaadhoo","kinolhas","maakurathu","maduvvaree","meedhoo"]}'::jsonb
