-- fares-maathodaa
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Faresmaathodaa Island?","answer":"Public ferry service operates weekly from Male (approximately 18-20 hours journey time). Private speedboat transfers can be arranged through guesthouses (approximately 7.5 hours from Male)."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Faresmaathodaa Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Faresmaathodaa Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. For whale shark encounters, visit during the southwest monsoon (May to December). Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year."},{"question":"What makes Faresmaathodaa different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Faresmaathodaa stands out for its exceptional preservation of traditional Maldivian life in a remote setting and its unique twin-island structure. Unlike most Maldivian islands, Faresmaathodaa consists of two separate islands connected by a small bridge, creating a distinctive figure-eight shape. This unique geography provides additional shoreline and beach access, while the channel between the islands creates a natural harbor and a special marine environment."},{"question":"Can I walk between the two parts of Faresmaathodaa Island?","answer":"Yes, the two parts of Faresmaathodaa Island are connected by a small bridge that allows easy pedestrian access between them. Walking across this bridge is actually a popular activity for visitors, as it offers excellent views of the channel and surrounding waters. The bridge has become a gathering spot for locals and visitors alike, especially during sunset when the views are particularly spectacular."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling around Faresmaathodaa?","answer":"Faresmaathodaa''s waters offer excellent marine biodiversity, including healthy coral formations with both hard and soft corals. Common sightings include reef sharks (particularly blacktip and whitetip), sea turtles, various ray species, and abundant reef fish. The channel between the two parts of the island creates a unique marine environment with different currents and marine life. Seasonal visitors include whale sharks (May-December) and manta rays. The house reef provides easy access to this underwater world directly from shore."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'fares-maathodaa';

-- feeali
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Feeali Island?","answer":"Public ferry service operates weekly from Male (approximately 12 hours journey time). Private speedboat transfers can be arranged through guesthouses (approximately 5 hours from Male)."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Feeali Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Feeali Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year."},{"question":"What makes Feeali different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Feeali stands out for its strong fishing tradition and authentic island life. Unlike more tourist-developed islands, Feeali maintains its traditional character with a community deeply connected to fishing. The island offers excellent fishing experiences and genuine cultural exchange away from mass tourism."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Feeali Island?","answer":"As Feeali is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas (shoulders and knees covered). Swimwear is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach.\" When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads. These requirements don''t apply during water activities."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling around Feeali?","answer":"Feeali''s waters offer good marine biodiversity, including coral formations with both hard and soft corals. Common sightings include reef sharks (particularly blacktip), various reef fish, and occasional sea turtles. The house reef provides easy access to this underwater world directly from shore."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'feeali';

-- feevah
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Shaviyani Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 600 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"0.7 km long, 0.3 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"280 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Pristine beaches, excellent fishing, peaceful atmosphere"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Nature lovers, cultural travelers, budget travelers"}],"island_overview":["Nestled in the pristine waters of Shaviyani Atoll, Feevah Island represents the essence of authentic Maldivian island life. This charming local island offers visitors a unique opportunity to experience traditional culture while enjoying some of the most beautiful beaches in the northern Maldives.","Feevah stands out for its untouched natural beauty, crystal-clear lagoons, and vibrant marine life. The island maintains its traditional character while welcoming visitors with genuine Maldivian hospitality and warmth.","What makes Feevah truly special is its peaceful atmosphere, excellent marine life, and the opportunity to experience authentic island culture. Visitors can enjoy budget-friendly accommodations, delicious local cuisine, and unforgettable underwater adventures."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Feevah Island is located in the northern part of Shaviyani Atoll, approximately 280 kilometers from Male. This remote location ensures an authentic and peaceful experience, far from the bustling tourist areas, while still offering excellent accessibility.","The island''s position provides natural protection from strong currents while maintaining access to some of the best fishing spots in the Maldives. The surrounding waters feature healthy coral reefs and abundant marine life."]},{"heading":"Feevah: Natural Beauty & Marine Wonders","paragraphs":["Feevah Island is renowned for its exceptional natural beauty, featuring powder-white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and vibrant marine life. The island offers an unspoiled tropical paradise perfect for relaxation and marine exploration."]},{"heading":"Pristine White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Feevah boasts some of the most beautiful beaches in Shaviyani Atoll, with soft white sand and crystal-clear waters perfect for swimming and sunbathing."]},{"heading":"World-Class Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef features diverse marine life, colorful corals, and excellent underwater visibility for memorable snorkeling experiences."]},{"heading":"Authentic Island Culture","paragraphs":["Experience genuine Maldivian hospitality and traditional island life in a peaceful setting away from commercial tourism."]},{"heading":"Pristine Sandbank Visits","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks for the ultimate desert island experience with picnics and swimming in crystal-clear waters."]},{"heading":"Beach Highlights","paragraphs":["Feevah''s coastal features include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The island''s underwater world features:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Feevah offers an excellent variety of activities focused on marine adventures, cultural experiences, and natural exploration. The island''s pristine environment provides perfect opportunities for both adventure and relaxation."]},{"heading":"House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Join local fishermen for authentic fishing experiences using traditional techniques and learn about the island''s fishing heritage."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Tours","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands and discover uninhabited sandbanks, each offering unique experiences and pristine natural beauty."]},{"heading":"Cultural Experiences","paragraphs":["Immerse yourself in local community life, learn traditional crafts, and experience authentic Maldivian customs and traditions."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy magical sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Adventures","paragraphs":["Discover world-class dive sites around Shaviyani Atoll with professional dive operators offering courses and guided dives."]},{"heading":"People & Community Life","paragraphs":["Feevah is home to a close-knit community of approximately 600 residents who have preserved traditional Maldivian ways of life for generations. The island''s population is renowned for their warmth, hospitality, and strong community bonds."]},{"heading":"Daily Life","paragraphs":["Life on Feevah follows the natural rhythms of island living, beginning with morning prayers and continuing with fishing, community work, and family activities. The island maintains a peaceful, unhurried pace that reflects traditional Maldivian values."]},{"heading":"Culture & Traditions","paragraphs":["Feevah preserves authentic Maldivian cultural traditions including traditional music, dance, and handicrafts. The community celebrates Islamic festivals with enthusiasm and maintains traditional practices such as dhoni building and traditional fishing techniques."]},{"heading":"Local Economy","paragraphs":["The island''s economy is primarily based on fishing and increasingly tourism. Many families engage in traditional occupations while also participating in the growing tourism sector through guesthouses, restaurants, and tour services."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Feevah Island?","answer":"Feevah Island can be reached by domestic flight to Funadhoo Airport (1.5 hours from Male) followed by a 30-minute speedboat ride. Seaplane transfers are also available but depend on weather conditions. There''s also a weekly public ferry from Male that takes 16-18 hours."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Feevah?","answer":"The best time to visit Feevah is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable. However, the island can be visited year-round, with the wet season (May-November) offering fewer crowds and lower accommodation rates."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Feevah?","answer":"Feevah offers various budget-friendly and mid-range accommodations including family guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages."},{"question":"What activities are available on Feevah?","answer":"Feevah offers excellent snorkeling from the house reef, diving excursions, island hopping tours, cultural experiences, traditional fishing trips, and sunset cruises. The island is particularly known for its pristine marine environment and authentic cultural experiences."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["foakaidhoo","feydhoo","bileffahi","noomaraa","narudhoo","milandhoo","maroshi","maaungoodhoo","lhaimagu","komandoo","kanditheemu","goidhoo","funadhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'feevah';

-- fehendhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Fehendhoo Island?","answer":"Public ferry service operates weekly from Male (approximately 10 hours journey time). Private speedboat transfers can be arranged through guesthouses (approximately 4 hours from Male)."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Fehendhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Fehendhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. For manta ray encounters in nearby Hanifaru Bay, visit during the southwest monsoon (May to November). Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year."},{"question":"What makes Fehendhoo different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Fehendhoo stands out for its exceptional preservation of traditional Maldivian life within the UNESCO Biosphere Reserve. Unlike more developed islands, Fehendhoo maintains its authentic character with a community still primarily engaged in traditional fishing and crafts. The island offers access to Baa Atoll''s spectacular marine life while providing a genuine cultural experience away from mass tourism."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Fehendhoo Island?","answer":"As Fehendhoo is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas (shoulders and knees covered). Swimwear is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach.\" When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads. These requirements don''t apply during water activities or at resort day visits."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling around Fehendhoo?","answer":"Fehendhoo''s waters offer excellent marine biodiversity, including healthy coral formations with both hard and soft corals. Common sightings include reef sharks (particularly blacktip and whitetip), sea turtles, various ray species, and abundant reef fish. Seasonal visitors include manta rays (May-November). The house reef provides easy access to this underwater world directly from shore."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'fehendhoo';

-- felidhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Vaavu Atoll, Central Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 2,100 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.8 km long, 1.1 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"66 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Speedboat or seaplane"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Magnificent culture, stunning beaches, excellent diving"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, divers, adventure seekers"}],"island_overview":["Felidhoo Island is a magnificent local island in Vaavu Atoll that offers visitors a vibrant glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. This exceptional island combines natural beauty with an energetic atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking outstanding cultural experiences and stunning tropical surroundings.","Known for its beautiful beaches, magnificent coral reefs, and excellent marine biodiversity, Felidhoo provides wonderful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s vibrant community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their dynamic way of life with magnificent hospitality.","What makes Felidhoo special is its magnificent natural environment and vibrant island setting. Visitors can enjoy stunning beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience dynamic island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the magnificent Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Felidhoo Island is beautifully located in the heart of Vaavu Atoll, approximately 66 kilometers from Male. This location provides a magnificent and vibrant experience while maintaining excellent accessibility to the capital and international airport through various transfer options.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to stunning coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Vaavu Atoll in its most magnificent form."]},{"heading":"Felidhoo: Magnificent Paradise & Marine Vibrancy","paragraphs":["Felidhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring stunning white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most magnificent marine environments in Vaavu Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in a vibrant, dynamic setting."]},{"heading":"Stunning White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Felidhoo features magnificent white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and dynamic beach activities."]},{"heading":"Magnificent House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers vibrant snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Vibrant Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the dynamic spirit of traditional island life with friendly locals and magnificent Maldivian culture in a vibrant community setting."]},{"heading":"Dynamic Sandbank Adventures","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks and magnificent islands around Felidhoo for stunning tropical paradise experiences with rich marine life."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Felidhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Felidhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Felidhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and magnificent activities. The island''s vibrant environment and dynamic atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a stunning, energetic setting."]},{"heading":"Magnificent House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in magnificent waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby stunning dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in magnificent marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, stunning sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Vaavu Atoll with vibrant exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in magnificent community settings."]},{"heading":"Dynamic Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience magnificent Maldivian island life with vibrant cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy stunning sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in magnificent waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Felidhoo is home to approximately 2,100 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and magnificent cultural traditions that create a vibrant atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Felidhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities. The island maintains a magnificent atmosphere where visitors can experience vibrant Maldivian culture and customs in their most dynamic, energetic setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this magnificent island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Felidhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and magnificent cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Felidhoo Island?","answer":"Felidhoo Island can be reached by speedboat from Male (1 hour 45 minutes) or by seaplane (25 minutes, weather dependent). Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Vaavu Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Felidhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Felidhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more magnificent local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Felidhoo?","answer":"Felidhoo offers various accommodations including magnificent guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a vibrant setting."},{"question":"What makes Felidhoo''s vibrancy special?","answer":"Felidhoo is known for its magnificent and vibrant natural environment. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering a dynamic atmosphere perfect for energetic exploration. Visitors can experience exciting cultural exchanges and participate in magnificent community activities."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["keyodhoo","thinadhoo","rakeedhoo","fulidhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'felidhoo';

-- fenfushi
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"What is the best time to visit Fenfushi for surfing?","answer":"The best time for surfing in Fenfushi is during the southwest monsoon (May-October), with peak conditions from June to September. During this period, consistent swells arrive from the southern Indian Ocean, creating ideal surf conditions. The largest and most consistent waves typically occur in July and August. Shoulder seasons (May and October) still offer good waves with fewer crowds. Outside of surf season (November-April), waves are smaller and less consistent but can still be fun for beginners or those looking for a more relaxed surfing experience. For more information about Maldives weather patterns, see our Maldives Weather Guide."},{"question":"Do I need to bring my own surfboard to Fenfushi?","answer":"While bringing your own board is ideal if you have specific preferences, Fenfushi does offer basic surfboard rentals through guesthouses and surf shops. Rental options are typically limited to standard shortboards and funboards (around 6''0\" to 7''0\") in reasonable but not perfect condition. If you''re particular about your equipment or need a specific type of board (like a longboard or step-up), bringing your own is recommended. Some guesthouses offer board storage for returning visitors. For serious surfers, consider bringing essential repair materials as well. If you''re traveling with multiple boards, check with your airline about sports equipment policies."},{"question":"What makes Fenfushi different from other surf destinations in the Maldives?","answer":"Fenfushi stands out from other Maldivian surf destinations in several ways. First, it offers a more authentic local island experience compared to resort-based surf camps, allowing visitors to immerse themselves in Maldivian culture. Second, the island is famous for its traditional boat building heritage, which is unique to this area. Third, Fenfushi''s surf breaks are less crowded than more commercialized spots, offering a more relaxed atmosphere in the lineup. Additionally, the island''s small size creates a tight-knit surf community where visitors can easily connect with locals and other travelers. Unlike resort islands, Fenfushi provides opportunities to experience genuine Maldivian life while still accessing world-class waves. For comparisons with other surf spots, check our Maldives Surfing Guide."},{"question":"Are there non-surfing activities available on Fenfushi?","answer":"Absolutely! While Fenfushi is best known for surfing, there are plenty of other activities for non-surfers or for when the surf is flat. The island offers excellent snorkeling right off the beach, with vibrant coral reefs teeming with marine life. Cultural experiences include visiting the boat building yards, watching traditional Boduberu drum performances, and exploring the island''s coral stone architecture. Fishing trips, sandbank excursions, and island hopping tours are also popular. The island has beautiful beaches for relaxing, and visitors can enjoy authentic Maldivian cuisine at local cafes. For those interested in diving, several nearby dive sites can be arranged through local operators. Check out our Things to Do in Maldives article for more activity ideas."},{"question":"What should I pack for a trip to Fenfushi?","answer":"Packing for Fenfushi requires consideration of both the tropical climate and local customs. Essential items include: surf gear (if not renting), reef-safe sunscreen, rash guard or surf shirt, hat and sunglasses, lightweight clothing that covers shoulders and knees for village wear, swimwear for the designated bikini beach, sandals or flip flops, basic first aid kit, waterproof bag for boat trips, and a reusable water bottle. For electronics, bring waterproof cases, extra memory cards, and universal adapters (Maldives uses UK-style plugs). Mosquito repellent and after-bite cream are recommended. If visiting mosques, women should pack a light scarf. Remember that Fenfushi is a dry island, so don''t bring alcohol. For more packing tips, see our Maldives Packing Guide."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'fenfushi';

-- feridhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Feridhoo Island from Male?","answer":"You can reach Feridhoo Island from Male by public ferry or speedboat. The public ferry operates three times a week (Sunday, Tuesday, and Thursday), departing from Male at 9:00 AM and arriving at Feridhoo around 2:30 PM. Some guesthouses also offer private transfers for a higher fee."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Feridhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Feridhoo Island is during the dry season from November to April when the weather is sunny with minimal rainfall and calm seas. The peak tourist season is from December to March, offering optimal conditions for beach activities and water sports. The wet season (May to October) sees occasional rain showers and slightly rougher seas, but still has many sunny days and lower prices. For the best balance of good weather and fewer crowds, consider visiting in November or April."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Feridhoo Island?","answer":"Yes, as Feridhoo is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas. Both men and women should cover shoulders and knees when walking around the village, visiting shops, or dining in local restaurants. Swimwear (including bikinis) is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach\" area. When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads with a scarf. These dress code requirements are a sign of respect for local culture and traditions."},{"question":"Is alcohol available on Feridhoo Island?","answer":"No, alcohol is not available on Feridhoo Island. As a local inhabited island in the Maldives, Feridhoo follows Islamic law which prohibits alcohol. This restriction applies to all local islands in the Maldives. However, if you wish to enjoy alcoholic beverages during your stay, some guesthouses organize day trips to nearby resort islands or uninhabited picnic islands where alcohol is served. Alternatively, you can visit the \"floating bar\" boats that anchor near some local islands, though these are not always available near Feridhoo."},{"question":"What activities are available on Feridhoo Island?","answer":"Feridhoo Island offers a variety of activities for visitors including snorkeling on the house reef, cultural village tours, traditional fishing trips, dolphin watching excursions, island hopping to nearby islands, sandbank picnics, and day trips to luxury resorts. Water sports like kayaking and paddleboarding are available through some guesthouses. Cultural experiences include Boduberu (traditional drumming) performances, handicraft demonstrations, and cooking classes. Most activities can be arranged through your accommodation or local tour operators on the island."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'feridhoo';

-- feydhoo-seenu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Seenu Atoll, Southern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 2,100 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.9 km long, 1.1 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"540 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Domestic flight to Gan Airport + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Splendid culture, gorgeous beaches, excellent agriculture"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, nature lovers, relaxation seekers"}],"island_overview":["Feydhoo Island is a splendid local island in Seenu Atoll that offers visitors an elegant glimpse into traditional Maldivian life in the southern region of the archipelago. This graceful island combines natural beauty with a refined atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking sophisticated cultural experiences and gorgeous tropical surroundings.","Known for its beautiful beaches, splendid coral reefs, and excellent marine biodiversity, Feydhoo provides wonderful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s elegant community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their refined way of life with splendid hospitality.","What makes Feydhoo special is its splendid natural environment and elegant southern location. Visitors can enjoy gorgeous beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience refined island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the splendid Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Feydhoo Island is splendidly located in the southern part of Seenu Atoll, approximately 540 kilometers from Male. This location provides a splendid and elegant experience in the southern Maldives, while maintaining good accessibility through Gan International Airport.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to gorgeous coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Seenu Atoll in its most splendid form."]},{"heading":"Feydhoo: Splendid Paradise & Marine Elegance","paragraphs":["Feydhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring gorgeous white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most splendid marine environments in Seenu Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in an elegant, refined setting."]},{"heading":"Gorgeous White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Feydhoo features splendid white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and elegant beach activities."]},{"heading":"Splendid House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers elegant snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Elegant Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the refined spirit of traditional southern island life with friendly locals and splendid Maldivian culture in an elegant community setting."]},{"heading":"Refined Agricultural Heritage","paragraphs":["Discover the island''s rich agricultural traditions and learn about traditional farming practices that make this community splendid in the southern Maldives."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Feydhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Feydhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Feydhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and splendid activities. The island''s elegant environment and refined atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a gorgeous, sophisticated setting."]},{"heading":"Splendid House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the elegant house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in splendid waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby gorgeous dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in splendid marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, gorgeous sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Seenu Atoll with elegant exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in splendid community settings."]},{"heading":"Refined Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience splendid Maldivian island life with elegant cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy gorgeous sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in splendid waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Feydhoo is home to approximately 2,100 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and splendid cultural traditions that create an elegant atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Feydhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, agriculture, and community activities. The island maintains a splendid atmosphere where visitors can experience elegant Maldivian culture and customs in their most refined, sophisticated setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and agricultural techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this splendid island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Feydhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and splendid cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Feydhoo Island?","answer":"Regular inter-island ferry services are also available between Seenu Atoll islands."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Feydhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Feydhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more splendid local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Feydhoo?","answer":"Feydhoo offers various accommodations including splendid guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in an elegant setting."},{"question":"What makes Feydhoo''s elegance special?","answer":"Feydhoo is known for its splendid and elegant natural environment in the southern Maldives. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering a refined atmosphere perfect for sophisticated exploration. Visitors can experience graceful cultural exchanges and participate in splendid community activities."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["feydhoo","maradhoo","hulhudhoo","hithadhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'feydhoo-seenu';

-- feydhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Shaviyani Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,800 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.7 km long, 1.0 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"195 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Seaplane or domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Spectacular culture, stunning beaches, excellent craftsmanship"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, craft lovers, adventure seekers"}],"island_overview":["Feydhoo Island is a spectacular local island in Shaviyani Atoll that offers visitors a remarkable glimpse into traditional Maldivian life in the northern region of the archipelago. This impressive island combines natural beauty with a stunning atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking extraordinary cultural experiences and spectacular tropical surroundings.","Known for its stunning beaches, spectacular coral reefs, and excellent marine biodiversity, Feydhoo provides wonderful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s remarkable community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their impressive way of life with spectacular hospitality.","What makes Feydhoo special is its spectacular natural environment and remarkable northern location. Visitors can enjoy stunning beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience impressive island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the spectacular Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Feydhoo Island is spectacularly located in the northern part of Shaviyani Atoll, approximately 195 kilometers from Male. This location provides a spectacular and remarkable experience in the northern Maldives, while maintaining excellent accessibility through seaplane transfers or domestic flights.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to stunning coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Shaviyani Atoll in its most spectacular form."]},{"heading":"Feydhoo: Spectacular Paradise & Marine Excellence","paragraphs":["Feydhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring stunning white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most spectacular marine environments in Shaviyani Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in a remarkable, impressive setting."]},{"heading":"Stunning White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Feydhoo features spectacular white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and remarkable beach activities."]},{"heading":"Spectacular House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers remarkable snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Remarkable Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the impressive spirit of traditional northern island life with friendly locals and spectacular Maldivian culture in a remarkable community setting."]},{"heading":"Impressive Craftsmanship Heritage","paragraphs":["Discover the island''s rich craftsmanship traditions and learn about traditional artisan practices that make this community spectacular in the northern Maldives."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Feydhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Feydhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Feydhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and spectacular activities. The island''s remarkable environment and impressive atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a stunning, extraordinary setting."]},{"heading":"Spectacular House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the remarkable house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in spectacular waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby stunning dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in spectacular marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, stunning sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Shaviyani Atoll with remarkable exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in spectacular community settings."]},{"heading":"Impressive Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience spectacular Maldivian island life with remarkable cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy stunning sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in spectacular waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Feydhoo is home to approximately 1,800 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and spectacular cultural traditions that create a remarkable atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Feydhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, craftsmanship, and community activities. The island maintains a spectacular atmosphere where visitors can experience remarkable Maldivian culture and customs in their most impressive, extraordinary setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and artisan techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this spectacular island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Feydhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and spectacular cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Feydhoo Island?","answer":"Regular inter-island ferry services are also available between Shaviyani Atoll islands."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Feydhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Feydhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more spectacular local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Feydhoo?","answer":"Feydhoo offers various accommodations including spectacular guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a remarkable setting."},{"question":"What makes Feydhoo''s spectacular nature special?","answer":"Feydhoo is known for its spectacular and remarkable natural environment in the northern Maldives. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering an impressive atmosphere perfect for extraordinary exploration. Visitors can experience stunning cultural exchanges and participate in spectacular community activities."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["foakaidhoo","feevah","bileffahi","noomaraa","narudhoo","milandhoo","maroshi","maaungoodhoo","lhaimagu","komandoo","kanditheemu","goidhoo","funadhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'feydhoo';

-- filladhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Filladhoo Island?","answer":"Due to the island''s remote location in the northern atolls, direct public ferry services from Male are limited. Most guesthouses can arrange the complete transfer from Male, including the domestic flight and speedboat connection. When planning your journey, remember that weather conditions can occasionally affect flight schedules in this region, so it''s advisable to allow buffer days in your travel plans. The journey to Filladhoo is part of the adventure, offering beautiful aerial views of the Maldivian atolls during the flight and a chance to experience the stunning blue waters during the speedboat transfer."},{"question":"What makes Filladhoo''s fishing traditions unique in the Maldives?","answer":"Filladhoo''s fishing traditions stand out in the Maldives because the island has preserved many traditional fishing methods that have been practiced for generations. The community continues to use sustainable pole-and-line techniques for tuna fishing, which minimizes bycatch and environmental impact. Night fishing using traditional hand-line methods remains an important practice, with knowledge of the best fishing spots and techniques passed down through families. The island maintains traditional boat building skills, with local craftsmen constructing and maintaining the wooden dhonis (traditional fishing boats) using techniques refined over centuries. Fish processing methods including drying, smoking, and making traditional Maldivian fish products like rihaakuru (fish paste) are still practiced. The community follows seasonal fishing patterns based on monsoon changes and fish migrations, demonstrating deep ecological knowledge. These preserved traditions offer visitors insights into sustainable fishing practices that have allowed Maldivian communities to thrive in harmony with the ocean for generations, providing a glimpse into an authentic way of life that is becoming increasingly rare in more developed parts of the country."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Filladhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Filladhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. This period is ideal for water activities, with excellent visibility for snorkeling and diving. For those interested in experiencing the island''s fishing traditions, this dry season also coincides with good fishing conditions, making it an excellent time to participate in fishing excursions with locals. The southwest monsoon (May to November) brings occasional rain showers but also lower prices and fewer tourists. This season can still offer good fishing opportunities, though sea conditions may be rougher on some days. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year. Due to Filladhoo''s northern location, it may experience slightly different weather patterns than southern atolls, with the possibility of brief rain showers even during the dry season. The shoulder months of November and April often offer a good balance of favorable weather and lower visitor numbers."},{"question":"What type of accommodation can I expect on Filladhoo?","answer":"Accommodation on Filladhoo is limited and simple, reflecting the island''s authentic character and minimal tourism development. The island offers a small number of family-run guesthouses that provide clean, comfortable rooms with basic amenities including air conditioning, private bathrooms with hot water, and Wi-Fi (though connectivity may be inconsistent). Most accommodations offer full-board packages that include three home-cooked Maldivian meals daily, featuring fresh seafood caught by local fishermen. Some fishing families also offer homestay experiences where guests stay in a room within a family home, providing deeper cultural immersion and the opportunity to participate in fishing activities. Luxury amenities are limited, and the focus is on authentic experiences rather than high-end facilities. What these accommodations lack in luxury, they make up for in personal service, cultural insights, and genuine hospitality. Visitors should adjust their expectations accordingly and embrace the opportunity to experience authentic island life rather than expecting resort-style amenities."},{"question":"Can I participate in fishing activities as a visitor to Filladhoo?","answer":"Yes, visitors to Filladhoo have excellent opportunities to participate in traditional fishing activities, which is one of the island''s unique attractions. Most guesthouses can arrange for guests to join local fishermen on various fishing excursions, from morning tuna fishing trips to evening reef fishing and night fishing experiences. Traditional pole-and-line tuna fishing demonstrations allow you to learn about and try this sustainable fishing method that has been practiced for generations. Hand-line reef fishing trips provide opportunities to catch various reef fish species while learning about local fishing grounds and techniques. Night fishing excursions are particularly popular, where you can fish under the stars using traditional methods while enjoying the peaceful evening atmosphere. Some accommodations offer more immersive experiences where visitors can participate in the entire process from catching fish to preparing and cooking them for meals. These activities provide not just entertainment but educational insights into sustainable fishing practices and maritime traditions. The level of participation can be adjusted based on your interest and experience, from simple observation to active involvement. Participating in these activities provides a unique experience not commonly available on other Maldivian islands while supporting the local fishing community."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'filladhoo';

-- finey
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Finey Island?","answer":"Due to the island''s remote location in the northern atolls, direct public ferry services from Male are limited. Most guesthouses can arrange the complete transfer from Male, including the domestic flight and speedboat connection. When planning your journey, remember that weather conditions can occasionally affect flight schedules in this region, so it''s advisable to allow buffer days in your travel plans. The journey to Finey is part of the adventure, offering beautiful aerial views of the Maldivian atolls during the flight and a chance to experience the stunning blue waters during the speedboat transfer."},{"question":"What makes Finey''s healing traditions unique in the Maldives?","answer":"Finey''s healing traditions stand out in the Maldives because the island has preserved a comprehensive system of traditional medicine that combines various influences while maintaining distinctly Maldivian characteristics. The island is known for its traditional healers (hakims) who practice diagnostic methods such as pulse reading and observation techniques that have been refined over generations. Finey''s healers maintain extensive knowledge of local medicinal plants and their applications, with some families specializing in specific types of treatments or conditions. The island has preserved traditional preparation methods for herbal remedies, including decoctions, infusions, poultices, and medicated oils that are created using precise techniques. What makes Finey special is the integration of Islamic healing traditions with pre-Islamic practices that have been adapted over centuries, creating a unique synthesis of spiritual and physical healing approaches. The community maintains specialized therapeutic massage techniques that differ from those found in other parts of the Maldives, with specific methods for different conditions. Finey is also known for its cultivation of medicinal plants, with some families maintaining gardens specifically for healing purposes, preserving plant varieties that have become rare elsewhere. These preserved traditions offer visitors insights into a holistic approach to health and well-being that differs from modern medicine while complementing it, providing a cultural experience that connects to centuries of Maldivian healing wisdom."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Finey Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Finey Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. This period is ideal for water activities, with excellent visibility for snorkeling and diving. For those interested in experiencing the island''s healing traditions, this dry season is also excellent as many medicinal plants are in bloom or fruit, and outdoor wellness activities can be conducted without interruption from rain. The southwest monsoon (May to November) brings occasional rain showers but also lower prices and fewer tourists. This season can be interesting for those interested in medicinal plants, as the increased rainfall supports lush growth, though some outdoor activities may be affected by rain. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year. Due to Finey''s northern location, it may experience slightly different weather patterns than southern atolls, with the possibility of brief rain showers even during the dry season. The shoulder months of November and April often offer a good balance of favorable weather and lower visitor numbers."},{"question":"What type of accommodation can I expect on Finey?","answer":"Accommodation on Finey is limited and simple, reflecting the island''s authentic character and minimal tourism development. The island offers a small number of family-run guesthouses that provide clean, comfortable rooms with basic amenities including air conditioning, private bathrooms with hot water, and Wi-Fi (though connectivity may be inconsistent). Most accommodations offer full-board packages that include three home-cooked Maldivian meals daily, featuring fresh seafood caught by local fishermen and sometimes incorporating local medicinal herbs in the cuisine. Some healing families also offer homestay experiences where guests stay in a room within a family home, providing deeper cultural immersion and the opportunity to learn about traditional medicine. A few properties are located near the beach, offering easy access to the island''s beautiful shores. Luxury amenities are limited, and the focus is on authentic experiences rather than high-end facilities. What these accommodations lack in luxury, they make up for in personal service, cultural insights, and genuine hospitality. Visitors should adjust their expectations accordingly and embrace the opportunity to experience authentic island life rather than expecting resort-style amenities."},{"question":"Can I experience traditional healing practices as a visitor to Finey?","answer":"Yes, visitors to Finey have excellent opportunities to experience traditional healing practices, which is one of the island''s unique attractions. Most guesthouses can arrange for guests to participate in various wellness experiences led by local healers. These may include consultations with traditional healers who can provide insights into Maldivian approaches to health and well-being. Medicinal plant walks allow visitors to learn about the various healing plants that grow on the island, their identification, and their traditional uses. Herbal preparation demonstrations show how medicinal plants are processed into remedies, from simple teas to more complex formulations. Some healers offer traditional massage sessions that incorporate local techniques and medicinal oils. Wellness workshops provide hands-on experience in creating simple remedies that visitors can learn to make themselves. For those with specific health interests, specialized sessions focusing on particular aspects of traditional medicine can sometimes be arranged. These experiences provide not just entertainment but educational insights into a holistic approach to health that has supported island communities for centuries. The level of participation can be adjusted based on your interest and comfort level, from simple observation to more immersive experiences. It''s important to note that these traditional practices are offered as cultural experiences and complement rather than replace modern medical care."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'finey';

-- fiyoari
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Faresmaathodaa Island?","answer":"Public ferry service operates weekly from Male (approximately 18-20 hours journey time). Private speedboat transfers can be arranged through guesthouses (approximately 7.5 hours from Male)."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Faresmaathodaa Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Faresmaathodaa Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. For whale shark encounters, visit during the southwest monsoon (May to December). Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year."},{"question":"What makes Faresmaathodaa different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Faresmaathodaa stands out for its exceptional preservation of traditional Maldivian life in a remote setting and its unique twin-island structure. Unlike most Maldivian islands, Faresmaathodaa consists of two separate islands connected by a small bridge, creating a distinctive figure-eight shape. This unique geography provides additional shoreline and beach access, while the channel between the islands creates a natural harbor and a special marine environment."},{"question":"Can I walk between the two parts of Faresmaathodaa Island?","answer":"Yes, the two parts of Faresmaathodaa Island are connected by a small bridge that allows easy pedestrian access between them. Walking across this bridge is actually a popular activity for visitors, as it offers excellent views of the channel and surrounding waters. The bridge has become a gathering spot for locals and visitors alike, especially during sunset when the views are particularly spectacular."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling around Faresmaathodaa?","answer":"Faresmaathodaa''s waters offer excellent marine biodiversity, including healthy coral formations with both hard and soft corals. Common sightings include reef sharks (particularly blacktip and whitetip), sea turtles, various ray species, and abundant reef fish. The channel between the two parts of the island creates a unique marine environment with different currents and marine life. Seasonal visitors include whale sharks (May-December) and manta rays. The house reef provides easy access to this underwater world directly from shore."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'fiyoari';

