-- mandhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Mandhoo Island?","answer":"Mandhoo Island is accessible via several transportation options. The public ferry from Male operates three times a week (Sunday, Tuesday, and Thursday), departing at 9:00 AM and arriving at Mandhoo around 2:30 PM. Some guesthouses also offer private transfers for a higher fee. When planning your journey, consider that sea conditions can occasionally affect boat transfers, so it''s advisable to have some flexibility in your schedule."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Mandhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Mandhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon (December-April), which generally provides the best overall weather conditions with less rainfall, lower humidity, and calmer seas. This period is ideal for snorkeling, diving, and beach activities. The water visibility is excellent during these months, making it perfect for marine life observation. The southwest monsoon (May-November) may have occasional rain showers but still offers many sunny days, fewer tourists, and lower prices. For farm tours and agricultural experiences, the period from January to March is particularly good as many crops are flourishing. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) year-round, making Mandhoo a viable destination throughout the year. If you''re interested in whale shark sightings in nearby areas, the period from January to April is best. For the most peaceful experience, avoid the peak holiday seasons of December-January and July-August when accommodations may be more limited."},{"question":"What makes Mandhoo different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Mandhoo stands out from other local islands in the Maldives primarily because of its strong focus on sustainability and organic farming. While many local islands offer authentic cultural experiences, Mandhoo has developed a unique identity centered around eco-friendly practices and environmental conservation. The island''s organic farms supply fresh produce to nearby luxury resorts, creating an unusual farm-to-table economy that''s rare in the Maldives. Mandhoo has implemented more comprehensive sustainability initiatives than most local islands, including renewable energy, water conservation, and waste management systems. The marine environment around Mandhoo is particularly well-preserved, with healthier coral and more abundant marine life than many more developed areas. The island offers a more tranquil experience with fewer tourists than popular local islands like Maafushi or Dhiffushi. Visitors to Mandhoo can participate in unique experiences like organic farm tours, conservation activities, and sustainable living workshops that aren''t widely available elsewhere. This combination of environmental consciousness, agricultural focus, and pristine natural beauty makes Mandhoo a distinctive destination for travelers seeking a more meaningful and responsible Maldivian experience."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Mandhoo Island?","answer":"Mandhoo Island offers a select range of accommodation options that emphasize sustainability and authentic experiences. Eco-guesthouses are the most common option, providing comfortable rooms built with sustainable materials and designed to minimize environmental impact. These family-run establishments typically feature natural ventilation, energy-efficient systems, and organic gardens that supply their kitchens. A few boutique lodges offer a more refined eco-experience with thoughtfully designed accommodations that blend into the natural environment. For travelers seeking an authentic cultural experience, several families offer community homestays where guests can live alongside local residents. Most accommodations offer package deals that include meals, transfers, and activities. It''s important to note that options are limited due to the island''s small size and commitment to sustainable tourism, so booking well in advance is recommended, especially during high season (December-April)."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling or diving around Mandhoo?","answer":"The waters around Mandhoo offer exceptional marine biodiversity, making it a paradise for underwater enthusiasts. The island''s house reef is particularly healthy due to local conservation efforts and limited boat traffic, featuring impressive coverage of both hard and soft coral species. Snorkelers and divers can regularly observe abundant reef fish including parrotfish, angelfish, butterflyfish, triggerfish, and fusiliers. Blacktip reef sharks are commonly seen, especially in the early morning and late afternoon, often swimming in the shallows near the beach. The area has a resident population of hawksbill and green sea turtles that can frequently be spotted feeding on coral reefs. Various ray species including eagle rays and stingrays are often seen gliding over sandy areas. Moray eels, octopuses, and various crustaceans inhabit the reef crevices, rewarding patient observers. Mandhoo''s proximity to the South Ari Marine Protected Area means that excursions to see whale sharks are possible, particularly from January to April. The waters around Mandhoo have experienced minimal coral bleaching compared to more heavily trafficked areas, resulting in healthier and more colorful reef systems. The combination of a well-preserved house reef and access to renowned dive sites in Alifu Dhaalu Atoll makes Mandhoo an excellent base for underwater exploration."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'mandhoo';

-- maradhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Seenu Atoll, Southern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 2,800 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"2.1 km long, 1.2 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"539 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Domestic flight to Gan Airport + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Magnificent culture, beautiful beaches, excellent fishing"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, fishing enthusiasts, adventure seekers"}],"island_overview":["Maradhoo Island is a magnificent local island in Seenu Atoll that offers visitors a vibrant glimpse into traditional Maldivian life in the southern region of the archipelago. This dynamic island combines natural beauty with a lively atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking energetic cultural experiences and beautiful tropical surroundings.","Known for its beautiful beaches, magnificent coral reefs, and excellent marine biodiversity, Maradhoo provides wonderful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s vibrant community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their dynamic way of life with magnificent hospitality.","What makes Maradhoo special is its magnificent natural environment and vibrant southern location. Visitors can enjoy beautiful beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience dynamic island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the magnificent Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Maradhoo Island is magnificently located in the southern part of Seenu Atoll, approximately 539 kilometers from Male. This location provides a magnificent and vibrant experience in the southern Maldives, while maintaining excellent accessibility through Gan International Airport.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to beautiful coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Seenu Atoll in its most magnificent form."]},{"heading":"Maradhoo: Magnificent Paradise & Marine Excellence","paragraphs":["Maradhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring beautiful white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most magnificent marine environments in Seenu Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in a vibrant, dynamic setting."]},{"heading":"Beautiful White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Maradhoo features magnificent white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and vibrant beach activities."]},{"heading":"Magnificent House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers vibrant snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Vibrant Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the dynamic spirit of traditional southern island life with friendly locals and magnificent Maldivian culture in a vibrant community setting."]},{"heading":"Dynamic Fishing Heritage","paragraphs":["Discover the island''s rich fishing traditions and learn about traditional maritime practices that make this community magnificent in the southern Maldives."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Maradhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Maradhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Maradhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and magnificent activities. The island''s vibrant environment and dynamic atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a beautiful, energetic setting."]},{"heading":"Magnificent House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in magnificent waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby beautiful dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in magnificent marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, beautiful sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Seenu Atoll with vibrant exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in magnificent community settings."]},{"heading":"Dynamic Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience magnificent Maldivian island life with vibrant cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy beautiful sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in magnificent waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Maradhoo is home to approximately 2,800 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and magnificent cultural traditions that create a vibrant atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Maradhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities. The island maintains a magnificent atmosphere where visitors can experience vibrant Maldivian culture and customs in their most dynamic, energetic setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this magnificent island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Maradhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and magnificent cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Maradhoo Island?","answer":"Regular inter-island ferry services are also available between Seenu Atoll islands."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Maradhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Maradhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more magnificent local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Maradhoo?","answer":"Maradhoo offers various accommodations including magnificent guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a vibrant setting."},{"question":"What makes Maradhoo''s magnificence special?","answer":"Maradhoo is known for its magnificent and vibrant natural environment in the southern Maldives. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering a dynamic atmosphere perfect for energetic exploration. Visitors can experience lively cultural exchanges and participate in magnificent community activities."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["feydhoo","hulhudhoo","hithadhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'maradhoo';

-- maroshi
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Shaviyani Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 800 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.0 km long, 0.6 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"218 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Seaplane or domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Serene culture, tranquil beaches, relaxing traditions"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, peace seekers, nature lovers"}],"island_overview":["Maroshi Island is a serene local island in Shaviyani Atoll that offers visitors a peaceful glimpse into traditional Maldivian life in the northern region of the archipelago. This tranquil island combines natural beauty with a relaxing atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking calming cultural experiences and serene tropical surroundings.","Known for its tranquil beaches, serene coral reefs, and relaxing marine biodiversity, Maroshi provides peaceful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s peaceful community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their relaxing way of life with serene hospitality.","What makes Maroshi special is its serene natural environment and peaceful northern location. Visitors can enjoy tranquil beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience relaxing island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the serene Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Maroshi Island is serenely located in the northern part of Shaviyani Atoll, approximately 218 kilometers from Male. This location provides a serene and peaceful experience in the northern Maldives, while maintaining relaxing accessibility through seaplane transfers or domestic flights.","The island''s position offers relaxing protection from strong currents while providing access to tranquil coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Shaviyani Atoll in its most serene form."]},{"heading":"Maroshi: Serene Paradise & Marine Excellence","paragraphs":["Maroshi Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring tranquil white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most serene marine environments in Shaviyani Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in a peaceful, relaxing setting."]},{"heading":"Tranquil White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Maroshi features serene white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and peaceful beach activities."]},{"heading":"Serene House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers peaceful snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Peaceful Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the relaxing spirit of traditional northern island life with friendly locals and serene Maldivian culture in a peaceful community setting."]},{"heading":"Relaxing Cultural Heritage","paragraphs":["Discover the island''s rich cultural practices and learn about traditional customs that make this community serene in the northern Maldives."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Maroshi''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Maroshi feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Maroshi offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and serene activities. The island''s peaceful environment and relaxing atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a tranquil, calming setting."]},{"heading":"Serene House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the peaceful house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and relaxing underwater visibility in serene waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby tranquil dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in serene marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, tranquil sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Shaviyani Atoll with peaceful exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in serene community settings."]},{"heading":"Relaxing Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience serene Maldivian island life with peaceful cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy tranquil sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in serene waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Maroshi is home to approximately 800 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and serene cultural traditions that create a peaceful atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Maroshi follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, culture, and community activities. The island maintains a serene atmosphere where visitors can experience peaceful Maldivian culture and customs in their most relaxing, calming setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and cultural techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this serene island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Maroshi has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and serene cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Maroshi Island?","answer":"Regular inter-island ferry services are also available between Shaviyani Atoll islands."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Maroshi?","answer":"The best time to visit Maroshi is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more serene local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Maroshi?","answer":"Maroshi offers various accommodations including serene guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a peaceful setting."},{"question":"What makes Maroshi''s culture special?","answer":"Maroshi is known for its serene and peaceful cultural environment in the northern Maldives. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering a relaxing atmosphere perfect for calming exploration. Visitors can experience tranquil cultural exchanges and participate in serene community activities."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["foakaidhoo","feydhoo","feevah","bileffahi","noomaraa","narudhoo","milandhoo","maaungoodhoo","lhaimagu","komandoo","kanditheemu","goidhoo","funadhoo"]}'::jsonb
