can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this vibrant island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Muli has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and vibrant cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Muli Island?","answer":"Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Meemu Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Muli?","answer":"The best time to visit Muli is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more vibrant local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Muli?","answer":"Muli offers various budget-friendly accommodations including family guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a vibrant setting."},{"question":"What makes Muli''s community special?","answer":"Muli is known for its vibrant and energetic community atmosphere. The island has a larger population that creates a lively environment while maintaining authentic Maldivian traditions. Visitors can experience genuine cultural exchanges and participate in community activities in this dynamic setting."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["kolhufushi","maduvvaree","raimmandhoo","dhiggaru","naalaafushi","veyvah"]}'::jsonb
